	"desc": "What Boki say (BokiLines, docs/BOKI_TALK.md). tuning: max_words = the most words in one bubble (punctuation and symbols don't count); act_words = the most words in one action, which a young Boki says after its name; bubble_s = seconds a bubble stays up; cooldown_s = seconds a Boki waits between lines (a trigger marked direct answers something you did and skips the wait); no_repeat = how many of its own last lines a Boki never repeats; min_lines = the fewest general lines a trigger may have; grown_stage = the speech stage (Care.speech) from which a Boki says lines instead of its name. tones = how a young Boki says its name, by feeling ({A} first syllable, {a} lower, {b} second syllable, {F} full name, {f} lower, {U} upper; KinSpeak.fill). sounds = noises a tone may use besides the name. alias = old trigger names that share another's lines. triggers: feel (a tone), word (the one word a stage-1 Boki adds), acts (what it does), lines._ (anyone) and lines.<element> (extra lines for a Boki of that element, the species' type).",
